items: js-long-accum-plus-hoisted-const-mixes-bigint
paths: file:v1/runtime/backend/js/src/main/scala/scalascript/codegen/JsGen.scala file:v1/runtime/backend/js/BUGS.md file:tests/conformance/long-accum-invariant-fold.ssc file:tests/conformance/expected/long-accum-invariant-fold.txt
scope: |
  JsGen's loop-invariant fold hoist (inlineForeachOrGenStat, ~JsGen.scala:3939-3941) builds its JS
  as TEXT: `let s = 0` then `acc = acc + _kN`. Both are raw JS `+`, so a Long (BigInt) accumulator
  throws "Cannot mix BigInt and other types" — bench.sh's list-fold js cell is n/a and the minimal
  repro dies where INT prints 165. Fix: when the accumulator or the addend is statically Long, seed
  the inner sum `0n` and route both additions through `_larith` (which also gives the 64-bit wrap
  the hoist needs to stay valid — addition is associative mod 2^64, which is WHY the strength
  reduction is legal). Int path unchanged, so the optimisation is kept.
  Gate: tests/conformance/long-accum-invariant-fold.ssc (+ golden) — lane-independent, named for the
  contract rather than the lane; it must cover Int acc (fast path kept), Long acc (the crash), and a
  Long acc that OVERFLOWS (checks the hoist under wrapping).
next: fail-first on the case, then implement, then smoke-ci
